Llamascopium (formerly Language-Model-SAEs)
https://github.com/OpenMOSS/Llamascopium
Authors: Xuyang Ge, Zhengfu He, Wentao Shu, Fukang Zhu, Lingjie Chen,
Junxuan Wang (OpenMOSS)

Declared as MIT in the project's pyproject.toml (`license.text = "MIT"`). The
project ships no LICENSE file and states no copyright line of its own, so none
is reproduced here; the MIT text below is the standard text of the license the
project names.

`neuronpedia_graph/crm_interp_engine.py` is derived from this project. It runs
llamascopium's Complete Replacement Model attribution against a HuggingFace
model hooked by interp-engine, instead of a TransformerLens `HookedTransformer`.
Specifically:

  * `InterpEngineLanguageModel.apply_saes` and `.detach_at` reimplement the
    splice and detach structure of `llamascopium/circuits/hooks.py` against
    HuggingFace modules.
  * The set of gradient-freeze sites follows `ln_detach_hooks` and
    `attn_detach_hooks` in `llamascopium/circuits/attribution.py`.

The attribution algorithm itself is not copied. `attribute`, `prune_attribution`,
`NodeIndexedMatrix` and the `SparseDictionary` replacement modules are imported
from llamascopium and run unmodified.

